WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Have you ever looked at a clock and watched its first second hang in place?

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
The clock hasn't stopped. A controlled study found a change in how the first moment is judged.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Rapid eye movements interrupt visual input. Our experience still feels continuous.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Scientists tested the timing—and what happened when the target appeared to move.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
A vivid perception is real as an experience. The explanation still needs evidence.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Start with the free twelve-minute experiment. If you want audio later, ask what the product actually proves.
